# SEO-Outreach-Report — required credentials
#
# Copy this file to a private location and fill in real values. The path used
# throughout the docs is ~/.config/seo-rescue/.env (chmod 600). NEVER commit
# the real .env to git.
#
# Run with: node --env-file=/path/to/your/.env script.js   (needs Node.js 20.6 or newer)
#
# All four values below are needed for the full 10-chapter PDF. Each one says
# what is missing without it. The fetch script does not stop when a value is
# missing: the affected calls fail and the report lacks that data.

# Sistrix API — for Visibility Index data
# Sign up: https://www.sistrix.de/
# API-Tier must allow at least `domain.sichtbarkeitsindex` endpoint.
# Without it: no visibility index and no 18-month visibility chart
# (chapter "Sichtbarkeit bei Google im Zeitverlauf").
SISTRIX_API_KEY=

# DataForSEO Labs — for live SERP rankings, backlinks, competitors
# Sign up: https://dataforseo.com/ (pay-per-call, ~1ct per call typical)
# Without it: no keyword rankings, no competitors, no backlink figures
# (the ranking, competitor and backlink chapters). Both values are needed.
DATAFORSEO_LOGIN=
DATAFORSEO_PASSWORD=

# Google PageSpeed Insights v5 — for Performance + CrUX data
# Get key: https://console.cloud.google.com/
#   1. Create a GCP project
#   2. Enable "PageSpeed Insights API"
#   3. Create an API Key (restrict to that API)
# Free. Without it: the PageSpeed calls fail, no data for the speed chapter.
GOOGLE_API_KEY=

# Other skills read other variables (not needed for this pipeline):
#   psi-weekly-cron-baseline   GOOGLE_API_KEY (same key as above)
#   competitor-deep-audit      DATAFORSEO_LOGIN, DATAFORSEO_PASSWORD
#   target-keyword-set         DATAFORSEO_LOGIN, DATAFORSEO_PASSWORD
#   gsc-deep-dive              GSC_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON (path to a service-account file)
#   ai-citations-tracker       OPENAI_API_KEY, PERPLEXITY_API_KEY
# Full table with cost per run: COSTS.md in the repository root.
